-## Measured semantics — out of scope
-
-This property of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` is recorded so the hook features that follow specify against real behaviour. This issue does not change it; that is a separate, out-of-scope change owned by no issue in this epic.
-
-- The `catch` gates `onError` on `error instanceof Error` ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L150](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L150)), so a rejection that is not an `Error` — a thrown string or object — bypasses `onError` entirely while still propagating to the caller.
+- `onError` is called for every rejection, regardless of whether the rejected value is an `Error` instance; a string rejection is wrapped in a new `Error` with the string as `cause`, so the hook is typed against `Error` while `error.cause` reaches the raw value, and the original rejection is thrown to the caller unchanged ([validated by: calls onError once with an Error wrapping the string as cause, re-throws the original string](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L32)).
+- A plain-object rejection is similarly wrapped, with the object preserved as `cause`, and the caller still receives the original object ([validated by: calls onError once with an Error wrapping the plain object as cause, re-throws it unchanged](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L60)).
+- An `undefined` rejection is also wrapped so `onError` fires even when nothing concrete was thrown, and `undefined` is re-thrown to the caller ([validated by: calls onError once with an Error wrapping undefined as cause, re-throws undefined](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L84)).
